{
  "source": "SHA-256 is defined in NIST FIPS 180-4. Merkle hashing in this lesson uses domain separation prefixes 0x00 (leaf) and 0x01 (node), a common convention used by systems like Certificate Transparency (RFC 9162). Expected values were computed from this repository's reference implementation (phases/09-hashes-commitments-accumulators/04-merkle-trees/code/main.py) to lock behavior.",
